WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.870
So yesterday, we played clips for you of this
absolutely ridiculous phone call that Donald

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:11.730
Trump made to the Georgia secretary of state,
asking them to find eleven thousand seven

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.690
hundred and eighty votes and then saying,
come on, guys, I just need 11000 votes to

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.350
win Georgia.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.999
And certainly that call is impeachable.

00:00:19.999 --> 00:00:21.779
Donald Trump should be impeached for that.

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.119
He's not going to be I don't think, anyway,
he could be impeached after leaving office.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:28.769
But it doesn't seem that there is a political
desire for impeachment.

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:33.140
But one of the very interesting things that
has come out of it is that Georgia Secretary

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.910
of State Brad Raffensperger, who was on that
call, he was the one being pressured and he

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:42.730
is a Republican being pressured to find a
way to give Donald Trump the state of Georgia.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:49.620
He said it's unlikely we would investigate
or investigate criminally or ask criminal

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.350
charges to be brought because we have a conflict
of interest.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:57.400
We were involved in the call, but it is certainly
something criminal investigation and possibly

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:02.340
even charges that an Atlanta area district
attorney could do.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.850
And this is once again, it's just the tip
of the iceberg of what we may see once Donald

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.060
Trump is out of office.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.740
And, of course, this should be investigated.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.939
Here is the Georgia secretary of state, Republican
Brad Raffensperger, explaining, since he's

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:20.859
involved in this, he really shouldn't be part
of the investigation.

00:01:20.859 --> 00:01:25.770
And he's right about that, but says that there
are others, including the Atlanta area district

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:30.149
attorney, that might be the right outfit to
investigate.

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:33.590
David Worley, a Democratic member of the state
election board, which Hugh Chair has asked

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.100
you to open an investigation into the call.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.149
Will you open that investigation?

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:43.950
I believe that because I had a conversation
with the president, also had a conversation

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:49.499
with our chief investigator after we did the
signature match order of Cobb County last

00:01:49.499 --> 00:01:50.499
week.

00:01:50.499 --> 00:01:51.499
There may be a conflict of interest.

00:01:51.499 --> 00:01:54.649
I understand that the Fulton County district
attorney wants to look at maybe that's the

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:56.369
appropriate venue for him to go.

00:01:56.369 --> 00:02:00.590
So the first question and we'll go through
this sequentially, the first question is what

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.280
crimes might Trump have committed here?

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.060
And it's actually a long list.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.780
And I'm not saying Trump will face charges.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:15.500
I'm saying the list of possible crimes is
long federal laws against solicitation of

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.320
election fraud, I would argue were broken.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.260
To prove it, you need to know intent.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.830
But and that is hard to prove.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.150
But just because something can't be proven
in court doesn't mean that, colloquially speaking,

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.320
you and I can't say yet.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:33.980
Trump did that a federal laws against conspiracy
to intimidate, threaten, injure or oppress

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.110
any person of rights secured by the Constitution.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:43.250
A Georgia state law against solicitation of
election fraud arguably was broken and Georgia

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:48.460
state law against willfully tampering with
an elector list, voter certificate, ballot

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:56.380
box, voting machine, tabulating equipment,
or to solicit others to commit such tampering.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:02.020
So, as I told you before, with other Trump
investigations, I don't think this is going

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.550
to go very far.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:07.400
But it may be yet another thorn in Trump's
side once he leaves office.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:13.370
I think the most realistic scenario is not
Trump ever gets perp walked in handcuffs,

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.060
not Trump is even ever criminally charged
with anything.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:20.990
I think the most likely scenario, if I'm being
just, you know, not hyperbolic, but but but

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:26.870
sort of conservative in my thinking with you
is there will be investigations into Trump

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:33.260
and his organization that will be a thorn
in Trump's side for years to come.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.290
Now, another interesting aspect of this.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:39.510
Why was the call recorded to begin with?

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:45.560
We know now that the Georgia officials on
the call did the recording and they did it

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.930
because of their knowledge that Donald Trump
previously has lied about the content of phone

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:51.930
calls.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.100
So the recording was almost like an insurance
policy for them.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.740
Assuming Trump would later lie about what
was said, they wanted a record to be able

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.600
to say, here's what was actually said.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.940
So it's all completely embarrassing.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.870
And, you know, if only we could have seen
this coming right.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:11.510
Like if back in 2016 when when we were all
sounding the alarm and unfortunately there

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:15.650
